Local adaptations:
- code is reformatted (4-space black style); docstrings and comments are trimmed.
- package import paths are rewritten to local relative imports; unused imports dropped.
- instructions.py: the unused ConstrainedStartChecker, RephraseChecker,
  KeySentenceChecker and RephraseParagraph checkers and _STARTER_OPTIONS are removed.
- instructions_registry.py: _MULTITURN, INSTRUCTION_CONFLICTS and conflict_make are
  removed.
- evaluation_lib.py: the file IO and report helpers (read_prompt_list, write_outputs,
  read_prompt_to_response_dict, print_report) are removed.
- instructions_util.py: download_nltk_resources() is added and runs at import; it
  downloads punkt/punkt_tab only when NLTK cannot find them. Upstream has no such
  function.

Checking or upgrading: because of the reformatting, a textual diff against upstream
is thousands of lines of noise. tools/check_vendored.py compares code only
(formatting, comments and docstrings ignored); at the pinned commit its output shows
exactly the adaptations above. From the repository root:

  U=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google-research/google-research/e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0/instruction_following_eval
  for f in evaluation_lib instructions instructions_registry instructions_util; do
    python tools/check_vendored.py "$U/$f.py" "benchmarks/ifeval/ifeval_lib/$f.py"
  done

To upgrade, run the same loop against the new commit, port the code changes it
reports beyond the adaptations above, and update the pinned commit here.
